  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Envisioning Belaku Bakes**\n\nI\'m starting to visualize a stunning website for Belaku Bakes. The core focus is clearly on showcasing their delectable menu. High-quality imagery of their cakes, brownies, and other sweet treats will be key. I need to make the menu easy to navigate and visually appealing, emphasizing the luxury aspect of this cloud kitchen.\n\n\n**Analyzing Belaku\'s Details**\n\nI\'m digging deeper into Belaku\'s specifics. I\'m focusing on the additional menu items, like cookies and cupcakes, that need clear display. I\'m also planning the contact form with pre-filled WhatsApp text for custom orders, so I\'m investigating how to implement that. The physical location is key, and I\'m looking for the address in the uploaded files to properly display it via a map. I need to find those documents first!\n\n\n**Assessing Available Skills**\n\nI\'m pausing to perform a skill check. I need to determine if any skills are relevant to the core task. I have skills like cloudsql-execute-sql, and cloudsql-setup available, but they don\'t seem applicable at first glance, since the user wants a simple site without a database, but I should re-examine this. I need to proceed based on whether the site needs a backend.\n\n\n**Deciding on Architecture**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the best site architecture. It looks like a client-only React app is the way to go, unless we want to include server-side Gemini. But, since the user didn\'t mention needing any API keys or databases and specifically asked for a minimalist design, client-only seems ideal. There\'s no need for any backend, which is great! No Firebase integration, either.\n\n\n**Refining User Contact**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the best user contact method. Generating a client-side WhatsApp link from a form is perfect! I am no longer considering using a Gemini API, as the user wants a simple, focused site. Image generation seems relevant, however.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I am going to check the workspace directory structure to see if there are any uploaded files, documents, or image assets that represent Belaku Bakes\' logo, brand, menu, or details, so we can display them perfectly. Let\'s explore the directory."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 629619772
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
