    thinking: "**Structuring Menu Data**\n\nI\'m now focusing on creating a `/src/data.ts` file for menu items. The goal is to keep code clean and modular. I\'m structuring entries for items like brownies, cookies, cakes, cupcakes, cheesecakes, and savory bakes, which should greatly improve organization.\n\n\n**Designing Data Structures**\n\nI\'m expanding the `/src/data.ts` structure to include specific details for each menu item. I\'m starting with a `MENU_ITEMS` list. Now, I have item names, descriptions, prices, and tags. I have also separated item by category, such as cakes and brownies. I am thinking of including egg-free options in my `brownies` category. I aim for clarity and completeness in the menu data representation.\n\n\n**Refining Menu Item Details**\n\nI\'m currently fleshing out the menu details, specifically for brownies, cookies, and cheesecakes. I\'ve added descriptions, pricing, and category assignments for each item, like the \"Caramel Ganache Walnut Slab\" brownie and the \"Thick Dark Chocolate Hazelnut Chunk\" cookie. I am also working on categorizing items and adding prices for items like \"Burnt Basque Caramel Cheesecake\" and the \"Classic New York Berry Jubilee.\"\n\n\n"
