    thinking: "**Analyzing PDF Uploads**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the uploaded PDFs. My initial assessment involves scrutinizing the screenshots and OCR data. I\'m prioritizing the menu details and symbols to ensure the website is corrected accurately, and I\'m looking at page one to see the logo.\n\n\n**Identifying Brand Details**\n\nI\'ve moved on to brand identification, analyzing the \"Belaku Bakes\" logo. It\'s a pink leaves wreath containing a chocolate cake with a candle, and under that the business name is in cursive. I\'m noting the service offerings: customized cakes, cheesecakes, cookies, brownies, cupcakes, and savories, along with Vaishnavi K.S\'s name. I also have the contact information: phone number, Instagram handle, and location in Hennur. I\'m comparing this to the second PDF, focusing on consistency and brand messaging. I\'m focusing on the cakes.\n\n\n**Cataloging Menu Items**\n\nI\'m now cataloging the menu. I\'m noting the cake flavors like chocolate and pineapple, with their corresponding prices for 500g and 1000g sizes. I\'m also capturing the brownie menu, specifying box sizes and prices for various brownie types like fudgy, peanut butter, and Nutella. I\'m making sure to factor in the customization fees that apply.\n\n\n**Detailing Price Points**\n\nI\'m now diving into the price structures for the brownies, breaking them down by size (medium and large boxes). I\'m noting the costs of fudgy, peanut butter, Nutella, and Biscoff brownies in various quantities. I\'m also capturing the cupcake menu with prices for mini, medium, and large sizes of different flavors.\n\n\n**Compiling Menu Listings**\n\nI\'m now incorporating cookies, cheesecakes, and snack items. I\'m noting specific flavors and sizes, along with pricing for each, from the provided data. I\'m paying closer attention to visual details and will reference the shop\'s logo. I\'m focusing on ensuring accuracy in my cataloging.\n\n\n**Replicating Shop Symbol**\n\nI\'m now focused on rendering the shop\'s symbol, aiming for an accurate digital replica. I\'m thinking I can model it with React and Tailwind, designing a CSS/SVG version of the candle-lit cake in a rose wreath with \"Belaku Bakes\" in cursive. I can\'t currently access a direct image from the filesystem, but I\'ve reviewed the directory listing.\n\n\n**Locating Image Resources**\n\nI\'m now searching the project structure. I\'m noting the presence of `package.json`, `src`, `tsconfig.json`, and `vite.config.ts`. I\'m also looking into the `/assets` directory for related files, but the PDFs are attached to the conversation, not stored locally, so I can use the visual information to create an accurate SVG rendering of the logo. I\'m focusing on that now.\n\nI\'m now formulating a plan to create the SVG! The logo design will be key. I have a clear visual concept. I\'ll focus on crafting an exquisitely designed CSS/SVG representation of the brand symbol/logo. The logo features a chocolate cake with dripping fudge, a candle, a pink laurel wreath, and \"Belaku Bakes\". I\'ll create a custom SVG component and start the design.\n\n\n**Crafting Logo Implementation**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the `BelakuLogo` React component for the website. I am focusing on detailed SVG implementation for the brand mark: the cursive \"Belaku Bakes\", the pink heart, the cake, the candle, and the wreath. I\'m choosing a soft pink for the leaflets with a color like `#E093AB`. I\'ve started the visual design and am looking at the `src/components/Navbar.tsx` file for integration. I\'ll make sure to review the menu images.\n\n\n**Clarifying Menu Integration**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the menu images. The provided PDFs offer textual menu details, not product photos. I\'ve re-evaluated that the PDF captures menu booklets with cream backgrounds, matching our color palette. To enhance visual presentation, I\'ll leverage a Unsplash image gallery *as matching bakes*, styled to complement the menu lists. I\'m re-verifying `src/data.ts` to ensure perfect menu matching.\n\n\n**Expanding Menu Options**\n\nI\'m now expanding the menu options to provide users with more specific flavor choices. I\'m focusing on allowing precise selection of cake, brownie, cheesecake, and cupcake flavors like \"Signature chocolate\" and \"Nutella.\" I\'m also ensuring the website\'s flavor selection is exactly like the PDF!\n\n\n**Refining Menu Presentation**\n\nI\'m now integrating cookie, savory, and sandwich options. I confirmed all items are in `data.ts`, so I\'m focusing on the visual interface. Instead of generic cards in `Menu.tsx`, I\'ll match the PDF by directly listing items with prices. I\'m focusing on displaying cake and brownie flavors as specifically detailed in the menu book.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Booklet**\n\nI\'m now focusing on creating an immersive digital booklet, replicating the PDF\'s menu tables. I\'m aiming for an engaging user experience, complete with high-quality visuals alongside menu details! I\'m planning to achieve this by using an *interactive selector* resembling the physical menu card. I am planning on using React and Tailwind.\n\n\n"
