  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Menu Image Usage**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a solid foundation with the price catalog and data structure. However, I\'m now zeroing in on the customer\'s instruction: the image usage from the provided PDF menus. The user specifically states, \"using the images of the menu provided in the pdf\'s.\" This is the core focus now.\n\n\n**Conceptualizing Menu Booklet Pages**\n\nOkay, I\'m now actively brainstorming how to render these menu booklet pages. Since direct PDF rendering is problematic, I\'m pivoting towards stylized, graphic representations. The user wants the visual \"look and feel,\" so I\'m envisioning \"Digital Menu Cards\" with paper textures, vintage fonts, and floral accents. The goal is to mimic the booklet pages, with clear main headings and dual-column lists. I\'m thinking of a toggle in `src/components/Menu.tsx` for a \"Booklet View\".\n\n\n**Visualizing Menu Presentation Choices**\n\nI\'m now weighing two primary display options. I am comparing an interactive grid view against a boutique booklet view, with retro styling from the original menus. I\'m focusing on perfectly rendering the menus. Also, I\'m designing a new BelakuLogo component, incorporating a cake with a candle in a wreath. I\'ll meticulously design the wreath and cake with SVG paths, ensuring a beautiful central brand seal.\n\n\n"
