  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Image Inclusion**\n\nI am now focusing on the user\'s feedback concerning image usage, specifically menu images and the shop\'s symbol from the provided PDFs. The core concern seems to be that the images are not being used as intended. I\'m carefully reviewing the code to ensure that the image data extraction and integration processes are functioning correctly, with the goal to incorporate these elements as requested by the user.\n\n\n**Interpreting PDF Image Data**\n\nI have a breakthrough! I realize the PDFs are essentially image files of the menu pages. They\'re designed like elegant catalog pages. Now, I\'m working to extract the menu item details, like flavours, from the OCR data and page descriptions, such as the cake flavours on pages 3 and 4. I plan to recreate the visual layout using this information, ensuring it mirrors the PDF\'s style exactly.\n\n\n**Designing Visual Menu Cards**\n\nI\'m now incredibly excited about the prospect of transforming the extracted data into visually appealing \"Digital Menu Booklet Cards.\" I plan to build a slider within `src/components/Menu.tsx`, that offers an elegant, high-fidelity replica of a printed booklet for each category. I envision soft pastel backgrounds, double-line borders, and symmetrical pink/rose hues for each menu item. It\'s becoming very clear how to enhance the user experience!\n\n\n**Crafting Detailed Visuals**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the visual details, aiming for a refined \"Bespoke Menu Booklet\" aesthetic. I\'m focusing on green branch leaf outlines in the corners, fine serif typography, and clean price columns. I am thrilled about the interactive hover action, which lets users click any menu item for immediate customization. My plan is to have a slider within `src/components/Menu.tsx`! I\'m creating the designs for an \"Interactive Card Grid\" and \"Bespoke Menu Booklet\", from what I see in the PDF. I\'m starting to build a replica of the PDF booklet. Page one is a chocolate cakes page!\n\n\n**Structuring Menu Pages**\n\nI\'m now outlining page structures for the menu. Page 1, I see that this will be the chocolate cakes section and page two will be fruit and butterscotch cakes. Each page will include a title, background and a \"Flavour\", size, and price breakdown. Footer text remains consistent as well. Page three is for brownie bites, with a different column format.\n\n\n**Organizing Page Data**\n\nI\'m now focusing on page layout. Page four covers medium brownie slabs, with flavour and box size columns. Page five features large elite brownie blocks, similar to previous pages. Page six details cream cheesecake slices, and slabs, with new columns. I\'m noting the column layouts for data integration!\n\n\n**Structuring Menu Categories**\n\nI\'m now organizing the final three pages, noting the specific category information. Page seven is Artisan Whipped Cupcakes, featuring flavour-specific prices for mini, medium, and large sizes. Page eight lists Pure Butter Boutique Cookies, detailing the \"Box of 8\" and \"Box of 15\" pricing. Finally, page nine presents Artesian Warm Savouries & Snacks, with each item and its respective price clearly outlined. The layout is all set. I\'m excited by this!\n\n\n**Refining Digital Menu Design**\n\nI\'m now fully committed to creating a visually stunning digital representation of the PDF menu. I\'m focusing on crafting an \"Elegant Boutique Menu Card\" design, complete with custom borders, rounded corners, and drop shadows, for each page within `src/components/Menu.tsx`. I plan to integrate page tabs (like \"Chocolate Cakes\", \"Fruit Cakes\") to make each page look like a digital menu booklet catalog. I\'ll meticulously rework the code, paying close attention to lines 11-140 in `src/components/Menu.tsx`. My goal is to exceed expectations with an authentic and beautiful digital rendering.\n\n\n**Implementing Menu Components**\n\nI\'m now focused on the detailed implementation within `src/components/Menu.tsx`. I\'ll create a digital menu booklet with page tabs for quick navigation. Each page will feature pink floral emblems, \"Belaku Bakes\" in script, double-line margins, and a structured table layout. I will include a \"Configure & Order this\" hover option for each item, linked to a CTA button that auto-populates the custom order form. I\'ll maintain the \"Visual Showcase Grid\" as a secondary view!\n\n\n**Structuring Page Data**\n\nNow I\'m creating arrays for each page to manage data precisely. I have begun constructing data arrays for pages 1 and 2, specifically \"Artisanal Chocolate Cakes\" and \"Premium Fruit & Butterscotch Cakes.\" These are structured with `id`, `title`, `category`, `baseId`, `tagline`, `columns`, and `rows` to map the layout perfectly. I plan to use this structure for each page.\n\n\n**Refining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now implementing detailed data structures. I\'ve built the array for the \"Premium Fruit & Butterscotch Cakes\" page, including all data points. Now, I\'m integrating the \"Brownie Bites\" array, accurately capturing flavours and pricing for each box size. The goal is to accurately represent each menu item with full visual design!\n\n\n\n**Integrating Menu Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating the data for the brownie slabs. I am focused on the \'Classic Medium Brownie Slabs\' and the \'Elite Large Brownie Blocks\' arrays. These are structured by flavour and size. My goal is to use this integrated data to accurately construct the visual elements.\n\n\n**Implementing Data Tables**\n\nI am now implementing data tables for \"Artisan Cream Cheesecake\", focusing on accurately structuring data for slices and slabs, including each flavour. I\'m building data for each page, and I have now successfully mapped the data and visual design, including the final cupcake, cookies and savouries pages. I am constructing data for each page.\n\n\n**Constructing Menu Tables**\n\nI am now structuring the data tables for the final menu pages. I\'m building data for the \"Artisan Whipped Cupcakes\", \"Pure Butter Boutique Cookies\", and \"Artesian Warm Savouries & Snacks\" sections, ensuring each item has accurate flavour, size, and price columns. The aim is to have a structured, visual representation of the menu. I have successfully mapped the data and visual design, including the final cupcake, cookies, and savouries pages.\n\n\n**Designing Savouries Section**\n\nI\'m now designing the visual representation for the savory snacks page! I\'m planning to make a CSS corner layout with double floral borders in #DF8CA3 for the visual booklet view. The aim is to create a delightful aesthetic.\n\n```\n<p><b>Savouries & Snacks</b></p>\n    <div>\n    <table className=\"table-auto w-full text-center\">\n            <thead>\n            <tr>\n              <th className=\"px-4 py-2\">Name</th>\n              <th className=\"px-4 py-2\">Info</th>\n              <th className=\"px-4 py-2\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n            </thead>\n            <tbody>\n            {props.data.rows.map((row, index) => (\n                <tr key={index}>\n                  <td className=\"border px-4 py-2\">{row.name}</td>\n                  <td className=\"border px-4 py-2\">{row.info}</td>\n                  <td className=\"border px-4 py-2\">{row.price}</td>\n                </tr>\n              ))}\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n    </div>\n\n```\n\n\n**Designing Menu Backdrop**\n\nI am now focusing on the background style for the digital booklet view, aiming for a pure, soft cream-beige backdrop (`#FAF6F0`) with an elegant double gold/brown border to match the PDF. I\'m reviewing `src/components/Menu.tsx` to determine the best method for complete file replacement to achieve the desired visual fidelity, focusing on the complete booklet view.\n\n\n"
