    modified_response: "I have successfully adjusted the app to match the visual assets and menu booklet pages from the PDFs with high-end digital precision. \n\n### What was updated and adjusted:\n\n1. **Official Shop Symbol Replication**:\n   - Built a high-fidelity `<BelakuLogo>` component that renders a scalable, stylized CSS/SVG representation of the official **Belaku Bakes logo** shown on Page 1 of the PDF. \n   - It captures the signature **pink floral/laurel wreath**, the **chocolate cake with fudge drips**, the **single lighted striped candle**, and the **cursive branding text** complete with the **trailing pink curly heart**.\n   - Swapped out the generic placeholder icons in the **Navbar** and **Hero section** for this official emblem.\n\n2. **Digital Booklet View (Default)**:\n   - Overhauled the Menu catalog in `/src/components/Menu.tsx` to present a custom **\"Booklet View\"** by default.\n   - This replicates the exact look, feel, and typography of the PDF menu pages: a cream page background styled with delicate double-line margins and **pink laurel emblems** in the corners.\n   - Organized the categories exactly like the sheets (e.g., Chocolate Cakes, Premium Fruit & Butterscotch Cakes, Brownie Bites, Medium Slabs, Elite Large Blocks, Cheesecakes, Frosted Cupcakes, Savouries).\n   - Keeps the columns aligned exactly with the printed booklet prices (500g vs 1Kg, Box of 8/16/24/36, etc.).\n   - Implemented an **interactive feature** where users can click any row on a booklet sheet to immediately configure that bake in the order formulation box at the bottom.\n   - Included a toggle to easily swap to a **Card Album View** if they want to browse through full-color food visuals with tags!\n\n3. **Geographic Localization Corrections**:\n   - Corrected the floating label on the Hero element to read **Hennur, Bengaluru** (matching page 2 and the contact details) instead of Koramangala."
