ream Cheesecake\" and their availability.\n\n\n**Confirming Cake Image URLs**\n\nI\'m now cross-referencing these image URLs. I am confirming URLs like the blueberry cheesecake image (`https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1524351199679-46cddf530c04?q=80&w=800&auto=format&fit=crop`) are active. I\'m prioritizing the reliable images, like the cupcakes, and double-checking the butter cookies URL as a basic step. I\'m working to select a dependable selection.\n\n\n**Selecting New Images**\n\nI\'m now focusing on adding new images. I\'m prioritizing butter cookies, gourmet bread, sandwiches, and a baker baking photo for the about page. I\'m verifying the image URLs for stability, considering options for each, and prioritizing those. I\'m planning to introduce an image error handler to gracefully handle any image load failures, showing a placeholder card.\n\n\n**Implementing Image Fallbacks**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing implementing robust image fallbacks. I realize a default SVG icon, such as the `BelakuLogoSymbol`, is a smart, user-friendly approach. I will utilize the `onError` event for the `<img>` tag to show a placeholder when images fail. This handles temporary or permanent image URL issues. Specifically, I\'m integrating this in `Menu.tsx`, `Hero.tsx`, and `About.tsx` to ensure graceful handling across the app. This is to complement revamping URLs.\n\n\n**Designing Image Fallbacks**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing a visually appealing fallback. I\'ll use an elegant, warm gradient with a bakery icon and the logo centered. I am inspecting image locations to determine where fallbacks are needed, and found these components: `Hero.tsx`, `About.tsx`, and `Menu.tsx`. I\'ll focus on `Menu.tsx`\'s `<img>` tag specifically, viewing from lines 553-561 for context.\n\n\n**Evaluating Image Components**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on image integration within `Menu.tsx` and the modal. I\'ve re-examined the code block in the modal, noting the `src` attribute is derived from `selectedItem.image`. I\'ll focus on replacing potentially problematic URLs from `/src/data.ts`, starting with the problematic brownie slab image. I\'ll need to locate or provide a suitable replacement URL for this image.\n\n\n"
