    summary: "To find an Unsplash photo ID, you typically need to navigate to the specific image\'s page on Unsplash. The photo ID is usually part of the URL. For example, in a URL like `https://unsplash.com/photos/PHOTO_ID`, the alphanumeric string after `/photos/` is the photo ID[1].\n\nWhile a direct search for \"Unsplash [keyword] photo ID\" doesn\'t immediately yield a list of IDs, the search results provide direct links to Unsplash photos that match your keywords. You can then visit these pages to obtain the photo ID from the URL.\n\nHere are some Unsplash photos related to your keywords:\n*   **Garlic Bread**:\n    *   A photo of garlic bread with herbs and cheese on a plate.[2]\n    *   A general search for \"garlic bread\" images on Unsplash.[3]\n    *   A close-up photo of garlic bread.[4]\n*   **Savory Pastry**:\n    *   A photo of savory pastry with fresh vegetables and dips.[5]\n    *   A photo of savory pastries with meat toppings.[6]\n    *   A general search for \"pasty\" (often a savory pastry) images on Unsplash.[7][8]\n*   **Savory Bread**:\n    *   While not explicitly \"savory bread,\" many \"bread\" and \"baked buns\" photos can be savory.\n    *   General searches for \"bread\" and \"sliced bread\" on Unsplash.[9][10][11]\n*   **Baked Buns**:\n    *   A photo of \"baked breads\" described as vegan healthy cinnamon raisin roll buns.[12]\n    *   Another \"baked breads\" photo, mentioning cinnamon buns.[13]\n    *   A general search for \"buns\" images on Unsplash.[14][15]\n\nTo get the specific photo ID for any of these images, you would click on the provided link, and the ID will be visible in the URL of the Unsplash page.\n\nSources:\n[1] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFag8PcQ_8CvazRRzoy7D1ckEAdiQwGt2cROZJrzAkmyqI6Ttiyc8hnBpWFCT-cNCo_ul4Bi79Qr83DCX625WPYuW_xjLoPEZIAo7CJRJrOdoJ59kAFDa7Ry7NUEWrXVpjGKGFt3iSVdDNd8CcupfoSpNISbjYBAwLxytWRzgam2NBH5uOsRvFy_I8H0zsXhw==)\n[2] [unsplash.com](https://ver