    summary: "A search on Unsplash.com for \"garlic bread\" or \"garlic-bread\" would directly display relevant photos on the platform. The provided search results detail various aspects of garlic bread, including its ingredients, preparation, and history[1][2][3][4][5].\n\nGarlic bread typically consists of bread, such as a baguette, sourdough, or ciabatta, topped with garlic and olive oil or butter, often with additional herbs like oregano, chives, or parsley[1][2][5]. It can be grilled or baked until toasted[1]. The preparation often involves slicing the bread lengthwise or partially through, spreading a mixture of softened butter, minced garlic, and sometimes parmesan cheese, then baking it until golden and crisp[2][3][5]. Some recipes also suggest adding garlic powder, paprika, or salt to the butter mixture[2][3][4].\n\nHistorically, garlic bread emerged from bruschetta in Italy around the 15th century, with its contemporary form originating in the United States as a typical Italian-American dish[1]. This may have occurred as Italian immigrants started using butter as a substitute for olive oil, which was less common in the U.S. during the first half of the 20th century[1].\n\nSources:\n[1] [wikipedia.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGMnidWHX3AITgJa7PeLc8dK3LTaos6E5zuUJsgaOLufmNTrOPkyTNBjhj_k7gNDmlprqeUfh6zGI2opc99hOBUlGLa_P5ibCzxCOrkHtb8WHoIRferpOb-3-XZITJSn6rYlC71Pg==)\n[2] [grandbaby-cakes.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHTWQUK3AWd7X-4d8CJ1eEGsqJse2BqcNhgw-Z92NB1SOY7JVtctLzHYFVGIeqNCBBuhozvv_j-FoiPYedKTBRFuY6p1wnYSgs502fcOEkxoO-VkNZp5M0Cu3f8RQ-wkhhPQKl50vb7hi5qG1MmrrEp0R8=)\n[3] [couponclippingcook.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHfv3b-5TVn6NDw1Xx7l7Ucd_zIX4vQ4H9rHaWaQEMkR4OS_zbm3dKfOd5_G4PmeMbIvXPFbCPomTGuH0sRBAen-JzTdYuk3VRRvGd3piIpk9Nm2Pu-uxEqHPRyZtkz4yGqLhVXym9s6SU_OJ5OlGCvFg==)\n[4] [recipetineats.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud