    summary: "The search results indicate that \"Korean Cream Cheese Garlic Buns\" are a popular street food item, also known as \"Yukjjok Maneul-Ppang\" (six-sided garlic bread) or \"Cream Cheese Garlic Bread\"[1][2][3]. These buns are characterized by being soft, often made with milk bread, and divided into six segments, resembling a flower[1][4][3]. They are filled with a lightly sweetened cream cheese mixture and then dunked in a savory garlic butter sauce, which often contains minced garlic, butter, mayonnaise, honey, and parsley, before being baked again[1][4][5][3].\n\nThe appeal of these buns lies in their unique combination of sweet, savory, tangy, and rich flavors, with a crispy exterior and a creamy interior[4][5][2][3]. They are a variation of garlic bread that gained significant popularity in Korea around 2019-2020[2][3]. Several recipes are available for making these buns from scratch, including instructions for preparing the dough, the cream cheese filling, and the garlic butter sauce[1][5][3].\n\nSources:\n[1] [mydiversekitchen.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF_nWT_7e9U606W2wPRHcRm1UTOm8w_8UsvxRagU713K0jUxZS5jW2oRI1HfQpF22PsRQFXKo82lXOL69e2V8btG9SBCe80NX5ACIMjPMTuDlCrljCgB4IGX6ibCvoZG1v-bhrtqLqoPMbB67IOBqSLsocQ1BGidyVr9ks=)\n[2] [mykoreankitchen.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHfJkTcQJh6CzXp0s2LJjXPFXGT92ulRHyXPrHVbx93GU_I8yXBryztUTAPrJV9dZ5N_kcKGhST92f6b34ZwWrIfoS_dJz9N3bcrKDENcgoG6YL8qtyxl4SnJC8IwWYG-Ih-Y3ddMX5Bn5i_n-qUy71Ak04m4fvKxM=)\n[3] [food52.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGBCHHsijjAs1-zw8c7vhLzOyA9rO2aH5EzfKayTnQz1IqP4DR5ChBuhpcxMt4d5r4C6vf8B9V6AjJJqS90uIopZKgg2h6qAar2T50r9_1sFb9DQwl3NI6kH90U3tZvN0mwf66o_rurTVZ4clJrOj-s5eFP8C2PU2V1ZPia)\n[4] [moribyan.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFcQrPzK5uBv1GIJOADCx100yLB3mIwMNGqUJvFKde0EXl87B3SFCNB5j-F6r8HI5cXWi686u0GtJWymC0kwoAi5UDim-Ij