    summary: "A search on Unsplash using the terms \"korean garlic bread,\" \"korean garlic bun,\" \"korean garlic buns,\" \"garlic cheese buns,\" or \"cream cheese buns\" is expected to yield numerous images of this popular Korean street food. Korean garlic bread is characterized by round buns cut into six wedges, filled with a sweet and savory cream cheese mixture, and then drenched in a rich garlic butter sauce before being baked until golden brown[1][2][3].\n\nThe dish, also known as \"Yukjjok Maneul-Ppang\" (six-sided garlic bread) or \"Keurimchijeu Maneul Ppang\" (Cream Cheese Garlic Bread) in Korea, gained significant popularity around 2019-2020[1][4]. Unlike traditional garlic bread, the Korean version offers a unique combination of sweet and savory flavors, with a soft, creamy interior and a crispy, golden exterior[1][2]. Common ingredients for the garlic butter include melted butter, egg, milk, sugar, Parmesan cheese, and dried parsley, while the filling is typically a sweetened cream cheese[1][4][2]. Some variations may also include mayonnaise in the garlic custard[3]. The six-petal cut allows the flavors to infuse deeply into every bite, ensuring a rich taste sensation[4][2].\n\nSources:\n[1] [tiffinandteaofficial.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEaUCVJuOnXNT3fFn4G36UM8DOQknCYYXr4nlQOWHH8TABXWzPuPJe65PKViS3RrJTt3eAjK7Ksg7R38owHts8X5lHXTozJpsFZ76DM1cEWTcv8Vdg3rfx83kHkfBtL9-vsz4ve8XJgmqfZCKc4aeP4)\n[2] [beyondkimchee.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHb13IgWn9Bv_eym4UA3aitAdDZl1zfkHmPJfhHdIzDLS_f8X--lOQ-rxqMQNbqR2pxc7SVyVHtadNO9CN4Xw1dqvguioaSxayKIGwdqxF5WZadtVD-YricVJv4PUe3yctBa6l14r7-CD_f1tZ1Yz8EBdzCAftw9kGs7Q==)\n[3] [cammienoodle.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFyU0rpSG9NQZ_7pxxdLjSuVIQs55FDEImMfthTJ2sjD20WOU0AlrPDpiqOQv_Aq9FFuOk1vV6Hb7OSz8tOy3scYv_Vop4azR4_-PZ3Tx_B-LAh4e78xKMOtDUFHnTDwzZ55rRkyTmeCsouBaIUAoInZmGE)\n[4] [mykoreankit