    summary: "Korean cream cheese garlic bread is a popular sweet and savory Korean snack featuring pull-apart bread filled with sweetened cream cheese and dipped in a rich, buttery garlic sauce[1][2][3]. This treat gained significant popularity in Korea around 2019-2020, with people often queuing to purchase it[2].\n\nThe bread is typically cut into a six-sided (yukjjok) pattern, allowing the cream cheese filling and garlic butter to seep into every section[2][4]. Common ingredients for the cream cheese filling include cream cheese, sugar, and sometimes heavy cream[1][4][3][5]. The garlic butter custard usually consists of melted butter, minced garlic, sugar, parsley, and often includes milk, eggs, or condensed milk[1][2][4][3][5]. Brioche buns or other soft dinner rolls are frequently used as the base[2][3]. After filling and dipping, the bread is baked until golden brown[1][3].\n\nWhile numerous images of Korean cream cheese garlic bread are available on various stock photo platforms like Shutterstock[6], iStock[7], Dreamstime[8], and Freepik[9], the search results did not yield any direct links to images specifically from \"images.unsplash.com/photo-\" for this particular dish.\n\nSources:\n[1] [theunlikelybaker.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFnnbzrDWledQzzHQd3nPN9RNpUi3u00MDS9w7RPqV_OnQ9ySS76ou8r2WhxEuLaalKZAbIPiBISkR_dai6RdYVRDuyKt_FQS78YhM683klGfW9MOHnK5A9qEpr6dSWYomZrzetrE95VBUu7KKoE48sjYpPNY4UHJ_-NIONQGG95w==)\n[2] [mykoreankitchen.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF-hIBOZrQFUTMUM_RKtGNfY6aj0dVY5xOS6eVM3A7soeIu5C3JH3EuMYHJL66aegT8-JZPF-6NmoWb6gGlNgRwvng_oDflCa-_90_swXuUp2dL2FkUJ4NfmMD_ZvyFH-wdfk6EaMaq_zO0mcjCJbZCAFtJCinDduc=)\n[3] [yejiskitchenstories.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEtwwCf252gUCt2oCpcV_1t8N_uu90SludXghuvYZa1-45vnHBAZIk6lchq3bNBIU3k0W039HTiC8f1Swsun0M6lrVD35K3ZuZsXQtL8P2NRzJh3ARS3SM1H43FwW_zzoTQxAot1emigbb-wuo8e9EEqQcE