    summary: "The search results indicate that \"Korean garlic bread\" and \"Korean cream cheese garlic bread\" refer to a popular Korean snack that originated in Gangneung City in Gangwon Province[1][2]. It is also known as \354\234\241\354\252\275 \353\247\210\353\212\230\353\271\265 (Yukjjok Maneul-Ppang) or \355\201\254\353\246\274\354\271\230\354\246\210 \352\260\210\353\246\255 \353\270\214\353\240\210\353\223\234 (Cream Cheese Garlic Bread)[3].\n\nThis bread is distinct from Western-style garlic bread. It typically features a soft milk bread bun, often segmented into six \"petals\" or \"leaves\"[4][2]. These segments are filled with a lightly sweetened cream cheese mixture and then the entire bun is generously dipped in a savory-sweet garlic butter mixture before being baked[4][1][2]. The final product is described as rich, garlicky, buttery, and luxurious, with a slightly crunchy exterior and a soft interior[4][1]. The combination of sweet cream cheese and savory garlic butter creates a unique and appealing flavor profile that gained significant popularity in Korea around 2019-2020[3][2].\n\nSources:\n[1] [bake-street.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHo4uwb83HMJ9Cr1GnUwrjU7GJPNEqTIVy7vJJLWO0e_WKHYCIb8u33F-WrAy_3SMVOSPEnFMYOgVbeM2ayyXRJOSt958oLKu7AFflPvD3cWEBVNgd8Hd93WDAgxNJJBdAYXvGRIP1ZamYqW_YNBdTkcQHauKMMSw==)\n[2] [mydiversekitchen.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHL4yfwDgHGv8TbFlg_L3FJxiYuU2RLIhXDocKN1YJqD5EvtVvUOi2EF47tHCUGviTVoodY5Qg2aOU3J79_nyHLQRot_DL3h6UOaGqXi3ucD2K64Y_0cGK1N0r79BlXNXYtY4sS7GaTV3K5wrvmt1Wj6tPAiTNEexQ0jU8=)\n[3] [mykoreankitchen.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEhNohcAnHupEYYpSZ-6jcyt8EbvQHjmWWLLin9PZxDvQte1b87a3vf_Ziqqp5V3BLdS4w17sZsBqdooysjmBhHf0a_wYWxvBfoJfygIlQhbt_S84eSNDyN9XgkF7qp5tnsGxZOQjvK5JcztGAqYaWLGFvmR029uqo=)\n[4] [food52.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHruAyF