    summary: "I couldn\'t directly search Unsplash for images using your specified keywords and exclusions. However, I can provide information about these types of buns, which often includes descriptions that might help you identify them on Unsplash or other image platforms.\n\n**Brioche Buns:**\nBrioche buns are known for being soft, buttery, and slightly sweet[1][2][3]. They are an \"enriched dough,\" meaning they contain ingredients like milk, sugar, butter, and often eggs, making them different from leaner bread doughs[1][4][5]. This enrichment contributes to their fluffy, tender crumb and delicate, golden-brown crust[4][3]. Brioche buns are versatile and commonly used for hamburgers, other sandwiches, or as dinner rolls[1][4][2][3]. They are valued for their ability to soak up burger juices without becoming soggy[1]. Some recipes involve an overnight cold fermentation to enhance flavor and make shaping easier[4].\n\n**Garlic Buns:**\nGarlic buns are typically savory rolls infused with garlic flavor. They can be made from various bread doughs and often incorporate garlic in a butter spread, or directly into the dough[6][7][8]. Some recipes use store-bought dinner rolls or hot dog buns as a base, cutting them to create crevices for a garlic butter mixture and cheese before baking[6][9]. Ingredients often include minced garlic, butter, salt, and sometimes herbs like parsley and cheeses such as Parmesan[6][7][9]. Korean cream cheese garlic bread is a popular variation that uses brioche buns filled with a sweet, salty, and tangy cream cheese, then dipped in a savory garlic butter sauce[10].\n\n**Cheese Buns:**\nCheese buns are savory rolls with cheese incorporated into the dough or as a topping. They are often soft and flavorful[11]. Common ingredients include flour, milk, butter, eggs, sugar, yeast, and shredded cheese, such as cheddar, mozzarella, or Parmesan[12][13][14][11]. Some recipes suggest adding onion or garlic powder to the dough for extra flavor[12]. Cheese buns can be eaten as a snack or used as burger buns[12][11]. A specific type, cheddar cheese buns, may feature a crisp, cheesy crust and a cheesy filling, sometimes with a mix of parmesan and cheddar[14].\n\nSources:\n[1] [girlversusdough.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEUFSEdftzGX4aghr7Xg7iYWPDkedEgojTP6SmAsLfNRCtO8kTvLRMJF-nO_0D_yqnAdHA1CF1-hdJQUSMd1fcyt082CLdS4jbXPUKJL9S_AnutAhCm8oQ3Tn9UvgQPDjjZO891YjsSTw==)\n[2] [belovedsbread.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEhGflhh_ZXaUbDUJPxZ793GT_AHsuv3EHT852Md9stpv-3LmYA5XKgDTcg3yzBNzOJXPD9Ds499mA7WID9ebYUzYrVl4HpX4BHSvjX_X5s-fIpQtsmyuDjj5yd5mUZ4tkbX8xe0ecZnQYN43vYOB1nZGw=)\n[3] [thepracticalkitchen.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGUB5A-dRMwGqrf1KDqLhZb9iFS4JS3oxsJPj0gU1TODHN-_qB2iPAOj8wNhrxAuM6QgT5Y1j0nGjZ8-H5NHfOKG8xkLDd2idQhYLcqwPu-XoaqrJUxL_HA_dkZhBlpnd3ZqqZwaBCSkM10JeeU_8I=)\n[4] [thekitchn.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG9QdceBhPCzwIE4Pkt7tbS0-8rTETcYwYmei8jOZdbAk46Li-bB-ugjTxUr3_WKBCOW8KQnMBz-rJvvdibK1vjHAoXl9YvcW4KmADGzIRpf_D4XORi0YHakjO4H7ZR5I4J7WOWWU8IeWWOx-Cj4lqp)\n[5] [pinchandswirl.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHfINOr5abDnuSKY6qiwdHqc-BZe5Mrc75HP4vdfkgAnNwpxDLUFjLMu_Tu5fkmavJTQ7alC88BfDHd0PL_Z4KSkcb77WZIlpE3icY9CX72FV7g8FJfV9tpWIsOHiTOJOd7mnHNtOT8lw==)\n[6] [theenglishkitchen.co](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFifYMW8o6NptHHE6LY-Cc3VgHQ56Uz9vUeQaXneuRsthWIzYBSiEDwP8Pt1qf-bvexAf1yob-3GuVDlUI0lPJZtDJxuqoyALWiYcZM4QC4goaMjVjasaAmLz92olcdoabV4RQCu3SOl1-zx--iRpHvZypRhEzZYg1jiQZsAeDm-W1V47BiI160n4JxrKo=)\n[7] [tastingtable.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFC1ZBZEdmyisN9agQJXAc2pkLsN_cycgqsE036mxG3HFa_6gcmwvHWXKlv7XVAs3ezmJdbC6aQZ38xjsd5TUDZPuO63DlMygCCaPtlC8M2XHCDpBrLG3kK5n9HMWo3PCRqMyVMW8RbuctPS04Aj_izG6OmiN7M_RU28Xx0xX__nbtC)\n[8] [rakskitchen.net](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHAExOPZggyHqv1X0Qd2RcZ0Z3PF96AOnyc1UO81O7LYBsGKzHCkXTtOXrkoTP694VycKJEbyIaIMgrDfk8znl4O57y57sc4KbMKudqQnbRM-oyf06Q7bTFJ9sNl7zD6bMFoXyajTfOYa0BHMTMTtbAtso=)\n[9] [thisoldgal.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF_LHNKXh7b3lKJm-UguLQ6ClypDWgGjiSJFVF5lyYrVKvgkMDBz91Yz1zqMYfFkCLtSW3ej6lg-Jcxw_U_8dm0VMGll85koKXmrmCrsASCOcMKEp2p3myCB0eMkiIgmYgMSW0KRT2r-Nup2uNNgA==)\n[10] [mykoreankitchen.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGtiIfdh39kc2aktBHRV8t17uJ4jXg8Aq0sVIFV2SAzSw-HNbs5Sba6j4r0ZuunPLDfo7D3bCT65QSpaVPZYlPSqjOviiY45EEwQSOd6sy0iGIEVe0i4PVyY5HVPo_Y7Ja7UzLBRinuVLXQUwE4xgUo2TUyt73aVfE=)\n[11] [milkandpop.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHW5BoAKlMqRACFVNoGzGzrzFJdyxlzjY_I-aVsGXJIzcodVRnqi--LSXq8UuMcjydTgvjr-CIEp8_ZPWPN77RwunxCxxCAExX2CLpLwMxB5C1IDTmhMJWQoyQIYKN6To3XU02jPhc=)\n[12] [carmyy.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGrp26wmES2MYtPXjblX7QvojkWM0CLFfudzF5JsWjaVCIQ0kd3FvCkcN656xrjEDGkSBhOywvH2SdsSm3tIpt6B1E_pRR2Eqi1ZreCMp2WCqO3xN-xpPOuaSrNqUaoooqYa_YClfVQ)\n[13] [williams-sonoma.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHhMafm_MwRaeD3_lP4W2ipBZ51-X6pvDXObwJnsK8kvHN6Z_-4rVTPZqYkkF2Sx6wdOGG0eNkmlRICmgAzahJhYcFbS5UZH8b97K5cTy4wfNP95PhZWmy-H9s88CTKYNK6AMZ7ccPbM35_w1u2Rf9bMyHZCivLGHy1Qw==)\n[14] [womanscribbles.net](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGmhDVwiVr562q8nQUpzuCK_Wm9LHADTscc4o2YDooXzTMSuiHhCjnnln7U9MZePPG3ntiWGwRslugYXdguilmVLRgjx6ED_yn-UMds2SVSkm16WUFgROXpWsjU9L4yi64Z-Bfj2djepZoAeYhGBQ==)"
