    summary: "You\'re looking for images of Korean buns or Korean garlic bread specifically from Unsplash. While direct image links aren\'t provided in the search results, information about \"Korean cream cheese garlic bread\" and \"Korean garlic buns\" is abundant. These popular Korean street food items are often described as a delightful blend of sweet and savory flavors[1][2][3].\n\nKorean cream cheese garlic bread is typically made with medium-sized rolls cut into wedges, filled with sweetened cream cheese, and then drenched in a garlic butter \"custard\" that often includes milk and eggs, giving the bread a moist and custardy interior[1][4][5]. The exterior becomes crunchy after a second baking[1]. This treat is known for its garlicky, slightly sweet, and balanced salty taste with a creamy and tangy finish[1].\n\nThe buns are frequently cut into a six-sided (or \"six-petal\") pattern, which allows the cream cheese filling and garlic butter to infuse into every bite, creating a unique and irresistible experience[6][7][5][8][9]. They are a popular snack found in bakeries and market stalls across Korea, gaining significant popularity around 2019-2020 after originating in cities like Gangneung and becoming a trend in Seoul\'s Gangnam district[6][7][4][8][3].\n\nSome recipes offer variations, such as making them without added sugar for a more savory profile[4]. The bread itself is often soft and pillowy, a common characteristic of many Asian breads[2][10][3].\n\nSources:\n[1] [twoplaidaprons.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHHP3BH4tElPnO0JUFkfsxlFfI1almM8fSdQNwlZLK1WuQu9CxUaCIewzzN0LyvaQDCmrI2dc3DhMopKuU8FG4_B9lSyv9KERMYEYtqfUGzXy3uPHPYBNmrUrdd854SeM7QVEhpFUD9l6GBzvHB-zjpTQpXLiQ3)\n[2] [manilaspoon.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEySjI3VbLrGU-dsrhLkPL2w5SsWswlLR0nLqyTv9X8OB9Ul2bL9DUrwEPLqpnCuvfSYPyWW9t1D-drUTZQc2MEfX9-IUgtw8vcMVJS2laT5pH7bKr8tRxSAEyTLInCPsbjnyx7fi0lx3Dtjglj5x19PRBY3hpJ)\n[3] [mydiversekitchen.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGN_780mnUp7vb8DLFZD-rbwTdIfgqjsVdpDaiy02uQBHXsrY29m5xhaW7z7Aln4_ds11cuZ-AaDw-NEZNYmRI_sX24wSJEdf_QudQsPLmQjeQBkPn7ujwN3dQZYw-TlsuH5wLCp6II9ObIjLWlMPVNV8Q_KBhdX9kLgw==)\n[4] [cammienoodle.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFikWpYi2xJnaQyxNZOveeRHGHScgGJ9p7zOcWfwcbdcyrAmCrdUYKG8-tuyN4YVnHl66p_BKQYW76imMAWYAIinHuldY26vOw3RjsGdt4FqUf2K9qP7CmF2Jz6alg43Pji3zCjd5548iswkoB61Y8UaB0=)\n[5] [beyondkimchee.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGYkQlpsLVbYxZ48VQrYmZaZxTleDQshZlwq_Cah4qUvT_JZrCIEKgeYVsULCyueDgvrYiN0sjZ4acIfHs85ZbDSoUbEtav3oRmC24cq4uWewN0lVzf_Hfja_wPfLK7kOPxCor4Bm5Wi0zyMVUQXg4g99otpbT2RbQD)\n[6] [mykoreankitchen.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEC0LcR978gGrW-Jt0AOml5q9tcRQIkN_QoDg29U16TuszhlBuuvxbuXOvx3gERAyTEKNEvS01bi6mJ5qKFg5DV9-clMfkO_hvd4K2F_6hRKBVSJxVKJjBSHW67CEpH4suzwQZTsh_CAxf52rijEu2ieQJ_jzsjjw==)\n[7] [karenskitchenstories.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHenCujk1YbrlpdqENcRBPgBlBRAr4UPDhwkmCiICuq-BPGsllDkan9nJXJKrpV5vWDfJG5HtjfDUaJS2_NMaElFld1TlqA4KMQaT2Ea7PfcUCs0bz1sOUtdslnezEfGXfAHlYdFLN6xigO3Vdpq-u0e-wbBmIsAhWxcgZh3lHODIsDtvuyMSl7LQ8t)\n[8] [thedeliciousspoon.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEREmq0_nR-CYiCyROb_X_Qo8lPTVQA6PYjDIFtKbXAg6TByNRbsmVswoBoY3p2FtShUaA10W6BFPaCeS22MS2jW_M83LqpmZG_MSB82YLQVelPaaRrsIT3JSSu0uaaOBZoa-_RIXAp66G4r-v8j62vCkwAVZqS3Jwd)\n[9] [breadexperience.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGMfLjJZFktgu78MRvtMfyKaZnaIsf3t8bzc_r7BfzP1AORrePN9vWOQ0Rr-9zhNL6Q4KOTbAfaqL5PL6co6o40uP0RmU-HKh_5_tMyA5iI0_rR7DPeA2_KWcltl4niP7scWiVS9tBwZEZEgGYXZkIAcrTIPnEr9pVnTg==)\n[10] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG4k2VoZn1KsBCHG4i9cTq4koLjq-0fs8chI06OA12HjwWsWc2jnuPkALf9h2v