    summary: "Based on your search for \"images.unsplash.com\" AND \"korean\" AND \"bread\" OR \"bun\" OR \"buns\" -pinterest, you are likely to find images of several popular Korean bread and bun varieties on Unsplash.\n\nThe most prominent type of Korean bread that appeared in the search results is **Korean Cream Cheese Garlic Bread**, also known as \"Yukjjok Maneul-Ppang\" or \"Six-sided Cream Garlic Buns\"[1][2][3]. This street food is described as a pull-apart bun filled with a sweet, salty, and tangy cream cheese mixture, and then dunked in a savory, buttery garlic sauce[1][4][3]. It\'s typically cut into a six-sided grid pattern[1].\n\nAnother common type is **Korean Egg Bread** (Gyeran Bbang), a popular winter street food. These are often described as little, fluffy oval pucks of bread topped with an egg, with variations including cheese and bacon[4][2]. The bread itself can be sweet and is sometimes compared to a corn muffin[4][2].\n\nYou may also find images related to **Korean Milk Bread** (Roll Ppang), which is known for being soft, fluffy, airy, and slightly sweet, often enjoyed as bread rolls or a loaf[5][6]. This bread is a staple in Korean bakeries[6].\n\nSources:\n[1] [mykoreankitchen.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHiTUr67Ouq7PGd4r_d-Ygj8HQu5XgXIYjjudO0WkCJUVSx217Atse_HTtS1oFzjZTxcRNwZMgnP4sJMl7Qe88JEd42E3MyH43hG8VLnqMMkhvb6FNGpkwDDvYd7edX-k24gXPJtG36OjBeLblApxLU6TjFX1X9XQ==)\n[2] [emmymade.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGBBX53d1zgBQRiqqT0sPzPnwMofIaWgc2lZUyOwCuH63_QVmeEA7waJVfxFRXlcNfWCbcxHaw_9DAMGCWlesLnq1RNh8XdTFgvvylh13fEA-A9kZoCxE9qkrVvb6vI_-5tqLRecCF44-eBA3gw-9eclGpUThEOxnq1jSQMzJBv9NZS2A8=)\n[3] [mydiversekitchen.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFTd5ttIbBCZ4Fw_AB7DtWjAsZ139hKosrY_XNwyW-VyikJcSyHp1o52YRGFn8E1L49sgCAgS6s5-lBq9GuavWz2IxQinASBnmqwn_zOUKyt57IzXPbpqntYQuKiYLCIwJfmhF6gX8z9zlyh3EKvOgAzhrLZFb5Llustw==)\n[4] [m